WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.132
In under two minutes, you will invite people to help run your contest.

00:00:04.132 --> 00:00:05.183
We start on the map.

00:00:06.085 --> 00:00:09.417
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.171 --> 00:00:13.593
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.593 --> 00:00:16.083
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:17.429
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.181 --> 00:00:21.397
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.397 --> 00:00:22.049
Tap Allow.

00:00:25.565 --> 00:00:28.060
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.278
See the three dots?

00:00:29.278 --> 00:00:29.826
Tap them.

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:33.392
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:35.084 --> 00:00:35.713
Tap Mine.

00:00:35.713 --> 00:00:37.662
These are the contests you run.

00:00:39.341 --> 00:00:41.363
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:41.363 --> 00:00:42.731
This is your dashboard.

00:00:44.617 --> 00:00:45.282
Tap Team.

00:00:45.282 --> 00:00:48.344
Co-organizers get the same dashboard you have.

00:00:50.404 --> 00:00:53.400
Type their email, and tap Add co-organizer.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:00.978
They get an email like this one, with one button to open the dashboard.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:04.799
Judges are added on the Judges tab.

00:01:04.799 --> 00:01:05.660
Tap Judges.

00:01:07.437 --> 00:01:10.409
Type a judge's email, and tap Add judge.

00:01:13.975 --> 00:01:18.375
Your judge gets an invitation like this one, with a button that opens their ballot.

00:01:19.377 --> 00:01:21.374
Next up: Announce winners.
